Groups of one (retail: the raid finder / premade groups make a group for a single player).
Apply by hand (context from your tree: Groups/Group.h, Groups/Group.cpp, Handlers/GroupHandler.cpp).

Why: LFGPlayerScript::OnMapChanged disbands any group of one on every map change (the raid finder's raid
was gone as soon as the player was moved into it), and the 3.3.5 client sees a group with nobody else in it as "not in a group" and sends CMSG_GROUP_DISBAND
(leave) - the group was gone at once and the raid kicked the player out ("you are not in the instance's group").
A group marked SetAllowSolo(true) (server/raid_finder.cpp) ignores that leave while its only member is inside,
and is not disbanded when a member leaves and only one is left.
Leaving such a group alone goes through the script ("RF_LEAVE_RAID"), not the client's party menu.

--- a/src/server/game/Groups/Group.h
+++ b/src/server/game/Groups/Group.h
@@ class TC_GAME_API Group  (public, next to ConvertToParty)
         void   ConvertToParty();
+        // custom: a group of one stays a group (raid finder, premade groups)
+        void   SetAllowSolo(bool allow) { m_allowSolo = allow; }
+        bool   IsSoloAllowed() const { return m_allowSolo; }

@@ class TC_GAME_API Group  (protected members, next to m_isLeaderOffline)
         bool                m_isLeaderOffline;
+        bool                m_allowSolo = false;

